 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "bava_metzia.48b.2",
   "daf": "48b",
   "sentenceId": 1,
   "he": "אֲבָל אָמְרוּ מִי שֶׁפָּרַע וְכוּ׳. אִיתְּמַר, אַבָּיֵי אָמַר: אוֹדוֹעֵי מוֹדְעִינַן לֵיהּ. רָבָא אָמַר: מֵילָט לָיְיטִינַן לֵיהּ.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches with regard to one who reneges on a transaction after the money was paid: «But» the Sages «said: He Who exacted payment» from the people of the generation of the flood, and from the generation of the dispersion, will in the future exact payment from whoever does not stand by his statement. «It was stated» that there is an amoraic dispute. «Abaye said» that «we inform» one who seeks to renege on a transaction: Be aware that this is the punishment of one who does not stand by his statement. «Rava said» that «we curse him» with that statement."
  }
 ],
